### Test Utilities
```typescript
// src/app/testing/test-utilities.ts
export class TestUtilities {
  static async configureTestingModule(options: {
    declarations?: any[],
    imports?: any[],
    providers?: any[]
  }) {
    await TestBed.configureTestingModule({
      declarations: options.declarations || [],
      imports: [
        HttpClientTestingModule,
        RouterTestingModule,
        ReactiveFormsModule,
        ...(options.imports || [])
      ],
      providers: options.providers || []
    }).compileComponents();
  }

  static triggerChange(fixture: ComponentFixture<any>, selector: string, value: any) {
    const element = fixture.debugElement.query(By.css(selector));
    element.nativeElement.value = value;
    element.nativeElement.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));
    fixture.detectChanges();
  }

  static expectElement(fixture: ComponentFixture<any>, selector: string) {
    const element = fixture.debugElement.query(By.css(selector));
    return expect(element);
  }
}
```

## 📊 Test Coverage & Quality

### Coverage Requirements
- Minimum 80% code coverage for services
- Minimum 70% code coverage for components
- 100% coverage for critical business logic

### Quality Gates
```typescript
// karma.conf.js coverage configuration
coverageReporter: {
  type: 'html',
  dir: 'coverage/',
  check: {
    global: {
      statements: 80,
      branches: 75,
      functions: 80,
      lines: 80
    }
  }
}
```

### Running Tests
```bash
# Unit tests
yarn test

# Unit tests with coverage
yarn test --code-coverage

# E2E tests
yarn e2e

# E2E tests in watch mode (headless false)
yarn e2e:watch

# All tests (unit + e2e)
yarn test && yarn e2e
```

## 🎯 Testing Best Practices

### Do's
- Write tests before or alongside implementation
- Use descriptive test names that explain expected behavior
- Test both success and error scenarios
- Mock external dependencies
- Use page objects for E2E tests
- Keep tests isolated and independent

### Don'ts
- Don't test Angular framework features
- Don't test implementation details
- Avoid complex test setup
- Don't share state between tests
- Avoid testing private methods directly
- Don't ignore failing tests

### Performance Testing
- Monitor test execution time
- Parallelize test execution where possible
- Use efficient selectors in E2E tests
- Implement test data cleanup
- Optimize mock services and data